==Faroese==

===Etymology===
{{root|fo|ine-pro|*bʰeydʰ-}}
From {{inh|fo|non|bíða}}, from {{inh|fo|gem-pro|*bīdaną}}, from {{inh|fo|ine-pro|*bʰeydʰ-}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|fo|/ˈpʊija/}}
*: {{rhymes|fo|ʊija}}

===Verb===
{{fo-verb|bíðaði|bíðað}}

# to [[wait]]

====Conjugation====
{{fo-conj-30|bíð}}

==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
{{root|is|ine-pro|*bʰeydʰ-}}
From {{inh|is|non|bíða}}, from {{inh|is|gem-pro|*bīdaną}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/ˈpiːða/}}
*: {{rhymes|is|iːða|s=2}}

===Verb===
{{is-verb-strong|beið|biðu|beðið}}

# {{lb|is|intransitive}} to [[wait]]
#: {{uxi|is|'''Bíddu''' eftir mér!|'''Wait''' for me!}}
#: {{uxi|is|'''Bíddu'''!|'''Wait'''!}}
# to [[wait for]] something {{+obj|is|gen}}
#: {{syn|is|bíða eftir<q:less formal>}}
#: {{uxi|is|'''Bíddu''' mín.|'''Wait for''' me.}}
# to [[abide]], [[undergo]], [[suffer]] (some fate, usually something bad) {{+obj|is|acc}}
#: {{ux|is|Karþagómenn '''biðu''' ósigur fyrir Rómverjum.|The Carthaginians '''suffered''' defeat at the hands of the Romans.}}

====Conjugation====
{{is-conj-s1|b|ð|e=e|mp=-}}

