==Old Norse==

===Etymology===
{{root|non|ine-pro|*bʰeydʰ-}}
From {{inh|non|gem-pro|*bīdaną}}. Ultimately from {{inh|non|ine-pro|*bʰeydʰ-||to trust}}.

===Verb===
{{non-verb|beið|biðu|biðinn}}

# to [[abide]], [[wait for]] {{+obj|non|gen}}
#: {{ux|non|bíð þú mín hér|wait for me here}}
# to [[suffer]], [[undergo]], [[sustain]] {{+obj|non|acc}}
# to be in store for, [[await]] {{+obj|non|gen}}
#: {{ux|non|fagnaðu, vin minn, því at þín bíðr eilífr fagnaðr|rejoyce, my friend, for eternal joy awaits you (sg.)}}
# {{lb|non|impersonal}} (there) to be, to be to be had {{+obj|non|acc}}
#: {{ux|non|hvárki bíðr þar báru né vinds blæ|there is felt neither wave nor breath of air}}

